    "id": "tea_darjeeling_himalaya",
    "category": "tea",
    "nameEn": "Darjeeling Single Estate ('Champagne of Teas')",
    "nameDe": "Darjeeling Hochlandtee ('Champagner unter den Tees')",
    "subtitleEn": "High-altitude Himalayan terroir, First vs Second Flush, famous muscatel aroma",
    "subtitleDe": "Himalaya-Steillagen auf 2.000m Höhe, First vs. Second Flush, berühmte Muskatellernote",
    "imageUrl": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1594631252845-29fc4cc8cde9?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
    "origin": "India (West Bengal / Darjeeling Himalayan Foothills - PGI)",
    "isImport": true,
    "abv": "0.0% ABV",
    "tasteEn": "First Flush: Floral, brisk, spring green grape, peach. Second Flush: Warm amber, ripe muscatel grape, nutty finish.",
    "tasteDe": "First Flush: Zart blumig, spritzig, grüner Pfirsich. Second Flush: Vollmundig, reife Muskatellertraube, nussig.",
    "scienceEn": "Darjeeling tea is cultivated on steep Himalayan slopes under intense mountain UV radiation and cool nights. First Flush (Spring harvest) leaves are only lightly oxidized (~20-40%), producing a liquor resembling fine oolong. Second Flush (Summer harvest) triggers defensive terpenoid compounds that generate the world-famous 'Muscatel' grape character.",
    "scienceDe": "Darjeeling wächst an steilen Hängen des Himalayas auf bis zu 2.000 Metern Höhe unter geschützter geografischer Angabe (g.g.A.). First Flush leuchtet goldgelb und schmeckt blumig-spritzig; Second Flush entwickelt das weltberühmte 'Muscatel-Aroma' – eine warme, traubig-nussige Note.",
    "culinaryEn": "Steeped at 90-95°C for 3 minutes. Served purely black in porcelain cups; never adulterated with milk or sugar.",
