    "scienceEn": "In Italian, 'macchiato' means marked, spotted, or stained. In busy Italian espresso bars, baristas needed a way to visibly distinguish for servers an espresso with a touch of milk from a plain black espresso. The small dollop of microfoam sweetens the initial sip with milk lactose and coats the tongue, muting initial bitterness without diluting the intense espresso concentration like a cappuccino would.",
