    "scienceExplainedEn": "Sunny Side Up is fried on one side only without flipping. Basting foaming butter over the white helps set the top without hardening the yolk. 'Over Easy' flips the egg for 15-20 seconds to lightly set the top while keeping yolk molten. Seasoning rule: Salt the white only, as direct salt on the raw yolk draws moisture via osmosis and creates white spots.",
    "culinaryServingDe": "Klassisch auf 'Strammer Max' (Graubrot mit Schinken), zu Bratkartoffeln oder auf Gourmet-Burgern.",
    "culinaryServingEn": "On burger patties, classic German 'Strammer Max' (rye bread, ham, fried egg), or English fry-up.",
    "guestFaqDe": "Warum salzt man das Spiegelei nicht auf den Dotter? Weil Salzkörner dem Dotter Feuchtigkeit entziehen und fleckige Stellen hinterlassen.",
    "guestFaqEn": "Why should salt not be sprinkled directly on the yolk? Salt draws water out of the yolk membrane by osmosis, leaving pale bleached spots."
