    "scienceEn": "Over 250 million years ago, ancient oceans evaporated and were sealed beneath tectonic rock strata. Mined deep underground (notably in the Khewra salt mines of Pakistan), this halite mineral is free of modern microplastics. The distinctive rose-pink hue comes from natural trace amounts of iron oxide (Fe2O3). With less than 0.1% moisture, it grinds razor-sharp in salt mills.",
